Which source files are derived
------------------------------

Derived files carry a header naming the upstream files they draw on.  The
distinction is not a judgement call: every file below cites upstream
file:line references in its comments, and the count is what decided it.

    src/mlx4_regs.h      123 upstream references -- register offsets, opcodes,
                         structure layouts taken from cmd.h, device.h, cq.h,
                         qp.h, mlx4.h and the mlx4_core sources
    src/Mlx4Hw.cpp        98 -- hardware operations modelled on mlx4_cmd.c,
                         mlx4_eq.c, mlx4_cq.c, mlx4_mr.c, mlx4_port.c,
                         mlx4_fw.c, mlx4_qp.c, mlx4_pd.c, mlx4_alloc.c
    src/Mlx4Hw.h          28
    src/mlx4_pure.h       23 -- capability decode and profile packing from
                         mlx4_fw.c and mlx4_profile.c
    src/cx3_abi.h         20 -- the shared ABI and its decoders, whose field
                         offsets come from the upstream structures
    src/Cx3Mlx4.cpp       37 -- IOKit glue, with ported logic from the same
                         sources
    src/Cx3Mlx4.h          4

Original work in this repository, with no upstream derivation:

    src/Cx3Mlx4UserClient.cpp, src/Cx3Mlx4UserClient.h
    src/Cx3Debug.h      (boot-argument gates and the console echo; the pattern
                         is borrowed from drivers named in its comments, but no
                         code is)
    src/kmod_info.cpp
    tools/              (build scripts, the control tool, the tests)

Not present, deliberately
-------------------------

No proprietary third-party binaries, no vendor kexts from any machine's driver
backups, and no firmware: the ConnectX-3 firmware lives in the card's own
flash.  See docs/PUBLISH-SCOPE.md, which is the authority on scope.
